                <pb facs="0733" n="633" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg633"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.48/1303: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the High Commissioner at
                        Constantinople</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-11-29T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 29,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>99. Your 590, 19th.</p>
                <p>Although thoroughly appreciating situation, Department regrets that under
                    existing regulations it cannot authorize consuls to visa passports any Russians
                    without reference here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
